  {
    "id": "comp-12",
    "number": 12,
    "title": "Abstract Class vs Interface (in C++)",
    "topicId": "topic-22",
    "headers": [
      "Aspect",
      "Abstract Class",
      "Interface (Idiomatic C++)"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "**C++ Keyword**",
        "Class with >= 1 `= 0` function",
        "Abstract class with **only** `= 0` methods (no native `interface` keyword)"
      ],
      [
        "**Data Members**",
        "Can hold state (`protected` / `private` fields)",
        "Zero non-static data members"
      ],
      [
        "**Implemented Methods**",
        "Can mix concrete + pure virtual methods",
        "Only pure virtual methods + `virtual ~I() = default;`"
      ],
      [
        "**Constructors**",
        "Often has constructors to init base state",
        "Usually no user constructor needed"
      ],
      [
        "**Design Role**",
        "Shared partial base (\"is-a\")",
        "Pure behavioral contract (\"can-do\")"
      ]
    ],
    "codeExample": "",
    "note": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "comp-13",
    "number": 13,
    "title": "Composition vs Aggregation",
    "topicId": "topic-27",
    "headers": [
      "Aspect",
      "Composition",
      "Aggregation"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "**Relationship**",
        "Strong \"has-a\" / \"owns-a\"",
        "Weak \"has-a\" / \"uses-shared\""
      ],
      [
        "**Part Lifetime**",
        "Tied to whole (part dies when whole dies)",
        "Independent (part outlives whole)"
      ],
      [
        "**Sharing**",
        "Exclusive to one owner",
        "Can be shared across multiple wholes"
      ],
      [
        "**C++17 Representation**",
        "`Part p_;` or `std::unique_ptr<Part>`",
        "`Part*`, `std::weak_ptr<Part>`, `std::reference_wrapper`"
      ]
    ],
    "codeExample": "class Car { Engine eng_; };                     // Composition (Car owns Engine)\nclass Dept { std::vector<Professor*> profs_; }; // Aggregation (Prof survives Dept)",
    "note": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "comp-14",
    "number": 14,
    "title": "Association vs Aggregation",
    "topicId": "topic-27",
    "headers": [
      "Aspect",
      "Association",
      "Aggregation"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "**Nature**",
        "General peer relationship (\"uses / interacts with\")",
        "Specialized whole–part relationship (\"has-a\")"
      ],
      [
        "**Hierarchy**",
        "No container/part hierarchy (`Doctor` <-> `Patient`)",
        "Clear whole & part (`Playlist` contains `Song`s)"
      ],
      [
        "**Ownership**",
        "None",
        "Weak / non-exclusive"
      ],
      [
        "**Multiplicity**",
        "1-1, 1-N, M-N",
        "Usually 1-N (whole to parts)"
      ]
    ],
    "codeExample": "",
    "note": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "comp-15",
    "number": 15,
    "title": "Aggregation vs Composition (Quick Lifetime & Ownership Focus)",
    "topicId": "topic-27",
    "headers": [
      "Question",
      "Aggregation",
      "Composition"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "**Can the part exist without the whole?**",
        "**Yes** (`Book` exists without `LibraryShelf`)",
        "**No** (`Room` cannot exist without `House`)"
      ],
      [
        "**Who calls `delete` / owns destruction?**",
        "External owner (NOT the aggregator)",
        "The whole object automatically destroys the part"
      ],
      [
        "**UML Diamond**",
        "Hollow diamond `◇---`",
        "Filled diamond `◆---`"
      ]
    ],
    "codeExample": "",
    "note": ""
  },
  {
    "id": "comp-16",
    "number": 16,
    "title": "Virtual Function vs Pure Virtual Function",
    "topicId": "topic-1",
    "headers": [
      "Aspect",
      "Virtual Function",
      "Pure Virtual Function"
    ],
    "rows": [
      [
        "**Syntax**",
        "`virtual void draw();`",
        "`virtual void draw() = 0;`"
      ],
      [
        "**Base Body**",
        "Provides a default implementation",
        "Usually no body (though out-of-line body is legal!)"
      ],
      [
        "**Base Instantiable?**",
        "Yes",
        "**No** (makes class abstract)"
      ],
      [
        "**Derived Override**",
        "Optional",
        "**Mandatory** for concrete derived classes"
      ]
    ],
    "codeExample": "",
